    "created_at": "2018-09-14T18:34:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-14T18:34:16Z",
    "body": "I think there may be cases where the call to 'allowed-to-use' and the actual determination of a policy violation are separated in the spec algorithms. For those cases, are we still going to need to have a separate \"report a violation now\" entry point, or is it okay to just call allowed-to-use again?  -- We could mention somewhere that allowed-to-use should be idempotent, so the result of the first call can be cached.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
